                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Crossing Souls is a 2D beat-em up style game that some people says heavily lean on the height of popularity of Stranger Things and I'd say that's fair though it tried something drastic for the story and introduced very depressing topics for a PEGI 12-rated game. I could even go so far as to say that the progression of the story was heading in the direction suitable for a mature audience and implications of certain themes were sidelined because of the age rating. As for the gameplay it's a traditional beat-em up that tried different things at once but by the end of it feels underwhelming because some elements of it left so much to be desired. The utilization of characters and items are not optimal in which i end up with so many unusables though it makes sense for the sake of discontinuity of usage later but perhaps the game just wasn't design to be big and deep enough to begin with. All i can say try it if it's on deep discount for those who likes the art style but proceed with caution for 2D beat-em up fans cause this game won't sate that hunger for formidable fights. 7/10.",
